  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>TP3-chapter05-q01</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>What is the result of these assignment statements?</p>
<pre><code>a = 25 // 10
b = 25 % 10
</code></pre>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>TP3-chapter05-q01</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>1</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<code>a</code> is <code>2.5</code> and <code>b</code> is <code>5</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The <code>//</code> operator does integer division, so <code>25 // 10</code> is <code>2</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<code>a</code> is <code>2</code> and <code>b</code> is <code>250</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The <code>%</code> operator computes the remainder after division, so <code>25 % 10</code> is <code>5</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<code>a</code> is <code>2.5</code> and <code>b</code> is <code>250</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The <code>//</code> operator does integer division, so <code>25 // 10</code> is <code>2</code>, and the <code>%</code> operator computes the remainder after division, so <code>25 % 10</code> is <code>5</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<code>a</code> is <code>2</code> and <code>b</code> is <code>5</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The <code>//</code> operator does integer division and the <code>%</code> operator computes the remainder after division.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>TP3-chapter05-q02</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>What is the result of these statements?</p>
<pre><code>x = 5
print(x &gt; 5)
print(x &lt;= 5)
</code></pre>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>TP3-chapter05-q02</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>1</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They print the values <code>True</code> and <code>True</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[If <code>x</code> is <code>5</code>, <code>x &gt; 5</code> is the same as <code>5 &gt; 5</code>, which is <code>False</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They print the values <code>True</code> and <code>False</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[If <code>x</code> is <code>5</code>, <code>x &gt; 5</code> is the same as <code>5 &gt; 5</code>, which is <code>False</code>; also, <code>x &lt;= 5</code> is the same as <code>5 &lt;= 5</code>, which is <code>True</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They print the values <code>False</code> and <code>False</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[If <code>x</code> is <code>5</code>, <code>x &lt;= 5</code> is the same as <code>5 &lt;= 5</code>, which is <code>True</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They print the values <code>False</code> and <code>True</code>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[If <code>x</code> is <code>5</code>, <code>x &gt; 5</code> is <code>False</code> and <code>x &lt;= 5</code> is <code>True</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>TP3-chapter05-q03</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>What is the result of calling this function?</p>
<pre><code>def hello():
    print('hello')
    hello()
</code></pre>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>TP3-chapter05-q03</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>1</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It prints <code>hello</code> once.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[After it prints <code>hello</code> once, it calls itself, which prints <code>hello</code> many times and then causes a <code>RecursionError</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It prints <code>hello</code> forever.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[After printing <code>hello</code> many times, it causes a <code>RecursionError</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It causes an error the first time <code>hello</code> tries to call itself.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[After printing <code>hello</code> many times, it causes a <code>RecursionError</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It prints <code>hello</code> many times and then causes an error.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[After printing <code>hello</code> many times, it causes a <code>RecursionError</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>TP3-chapter05-q04</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>What kind of operator is <code>or</code>?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>TP3-chapter05-q04</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>1</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[arithmetic]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<code>or</code> is a logical operator, along with <code>and</code> and <code>not</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[bitwise]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<code>or</code> is a logical operator, along with <code>and</code> and <code>not</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[relational]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<code>or</code> is a logical operator, along with <code>and</code> and <code>not</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[logical]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<code>or</code> is a logical operator, along with <code>and</code> and <code>not</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>TP3-chapter05-q05</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Here is the function from one of the exercises in this chapter.</p>
<pre><code>def recurse(n, s):
    if n == 0:
        print(s)
    else:
        recurse(n-1, n+s)
</code></pre>
<p>What happens if you call it like this: <code>recurse(-1, 0)</code>?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>TP3-chapter05-q05</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>1</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It prints <code>-1</code>.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[It only prints when <code>n</code> is <code>0</code>, and <code>n</code> goes -1, -2, -3, and so on, so it never gets there.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It prints <code>0</code>.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[It would print <code>0</code> only if it reached the base case, but starting from <code>-1</code>, subtracting 1 never makes <code>n</code> equal to <code>0</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It does nothing, because <code>n</code> is not positive.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[The condition is <code>n == 0</code>, not <code>n &lt;= 0</code>, so a negative <code>n</code> doesn't stop the recursion; it goes to the <code>else</code> branch and makes a recursive call.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It prints nothing and causes a <code>RecursionError</code>.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Because <code>n</code> never equals <code>0</code>, the base case never runs; the recursion goes on until Python reaches its limit on the number of frames and raises a <code>RecursionError</code>.]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
</quiz>
